#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Wrong-tree guard (2026-08-27).
#
# The primary working directory of the agent shell is the MAIN CHECKOUT
# (/home/tarstars/prj/troll_farm), and the shell resets to it between commands.
# A command that forgets its own `cd` therefore edits and commits in the checkout
# instead of the agent's worktree — and because worktrees share refs, the commit
# lands on `main` and looks half-successful. That happened four times on the night
# of 2026-08-26/27 (a quarantine edit, a seen-state commit, a task charter, a
# cherry-pick), each costing minutes of forensics, and once costing the collector's
# regenerated stats file while repairing it.
#
# This hook makes the mistake loud instead of silent: no commit may be created in
# the main checkout. The checkout exists to host the 05:17 collector cron, which
# never commits. Everything else belongs in an agent worktree on `agent/<id>`.
#
# Deliberate exception: set TROLL_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT=1 for the rare intentional case
# (and say why in the commit message).
set -euo pipefail

TOP="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null || echo '')"
MAIN_CHECKOUT="/home/tarstars/prj/troll_farm"

if [ "$TOP" = "$MAIN_CHECKOUT" ] && [ "${TROLL_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT:-0}" != "1" ]; then
    cat >&2 <<'MSG'
refusing to commit in the main checkout (/home/tarstars/prj/troll_farm).

This is almost always a forgotten `cd`: the shell resets here between commands.
Commit from your agent worktree instead, e.g.

    cd /home/tarstars/prj/troll_farm-local_claude_1 && git add … && git commit …

The main checkout hosts the collector cron and is kept identical to origin/main.
If you really mean to commit here, re-run with TROLL_ALLOW_MAIN_COMMIT=1 and say
why in the message.
MSG
    exit 1
fi
